 steps:["Boil the orzo in salted water until tender and drain. Season the chicken with Italian seasoning, garlic powder, salt and pepper and dust lightly with flour.","Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat and cook the cutlets until golden and 165°F inside, 3 to 4 minutes per side. Move to a plate.","Melt the butter, add the asparagus with a pinch of salt and cook until crisp-tender, 3 to 4 minutes. Add the garlic for 30 seconds.","Whisk in the broth, milk, Dijon and lemon zest and simmer until slightly thickened, 3 to 4 minutes. Off the heat, stir in the Parmesan and lemon juice.","Return the chicken to the sauce to warm through and serve over the orzo."],
 tip:"Add the lemon juice off the heat at the very end; it keeps the milk sauce from curdling and the lemon tasting fresh.",
 st:[4,2,"Reheat covered at 70% power with a spoon of broth, 2 minutes."],
